## Two different "MCP"s — do not confuse them

### 1. Internal MCP — Master Control Program (legacy)
- `src/mcp/mcp_handler.rs` — `MCP` struct: internal priority routing over the bus
- `MCP::decide(msg)` — Prioritize high-urgency messages
- This is Helix's own internal concept, predating Model Context Protocol adoption

### 2. Model Context Protocol (MCP) — external tool servers
- `src/mcp_client/` — MCP client manager (`manager.rs`, `naming.rs`, `mod.rs`)
- `src/chat_command/mcp_handler.rs` — Chat-command MCP path (`how: "mcp"`, `to` required, read-only in v1)
- `src/config/mcp.rs` — MCP server config (`[mcp.servers]`)
- `src/chat_mcp_install.rs` — chat-mcp installer hook
- Live servers: `google` (gmail_search/gmail_read/calendar_list via google-mcp), `chat` (chat_read/rooms/health via chat-mcp)
- Note: google-mcp on the R630 is currently not answering tool calls (found 2026-11-08)

## ACP — Agent Client Protocol
- `src/acp/` — ACP server: `mod.rs`, `server.rs`, `protocol.rs`, `agent.rs`, `tools.rs`, `elicitation.rs`, `status_bar.rs`
- `src/config/acp.rs` — ACP config

## Chat-Command Loop (uses both)
- `src/chat_command/` — `mod.rs`, `envelope.rs`, `executor.rs`, `task_handler.rs`, `mcp_handler.rs`, `config.rs`, `reply.rs`, `state.rs`, `asus.rs`
- `!` JSON envelope (`how`/`to`/`which`/`time`/`scope`); `to` addressing (task 318); MCP path (task 319)
- `src/a2a/` — Agent-to-Agent protocol (`a2a_handler.rs`, `tasks.rs`, `types.rs`)

## Cron (background tasks — not MCP/ACP, listed here for context)
- `src/cron/` — Cron scheduler (`mod.rs`, `registry.rs`)
- Cron publishes `agent_run` for maintenance; hourly maintenance triggers

